  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1243 AM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nChilly temperatures are expected on Monday with cloudy skies over \nthe area. Cool, moist air will be wedged in with a strong surface \nhigh centered over the Ohio Valley and surface ridge extending \nsouthwest into Texas. Temperatures should only climb several degrees \nduring the day with afternoon highs mostly in the upper 40s to \naround 50. Lower 50s are anticipated in the southwest part of our \narea (Crockett County). Some patchy drizzle/fog is possible in the \nmorning, mainly in northern and eastern parts of the area. \n\nWinds will become southeast to south Tuesday with southerly low-\nlevel flow continuing through the rest of the work week. Overall,\nmostly cloudy skies are expected for our area each day as \nconsiderable low-level moisture persists. Despite the cloud cover,\nthe southerly low-level flow will facilitate a warming trend \nbeginning Tuesday. Highs are expected to reach the mid to upper \n60s Wednesday, upper 60s and lower 70s Thursday, and upper 60s to \nmid 70s Friday. Morning lows in the 40s Tuesday are expected to \nincrease to the mid/upper 50s by Thursday and then remain mild \nFriday and Saturday. \n\nBlend of models has sporadic low PoPs Wednesday into Friday (15-30\npercent), but confidence is low in any meaningful rainfall. An \nupper trough is progged to track northeast into the central and \nnorthern Plains around midweek, but associated lift will be well \nnorth of our area. The next main chance of rain looks to be \nSaturday, when a cold front is forecast to move south into our \narea.",
